IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 17 -- Fraudulent deeds, mischief and criminal trespass`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 421, 422, 423, 424, 425, 427, 428, 435, 436, 437, 438, 439,
-- 440, 441, 442, 449, 450, 451, 452, 453, 459, 460, 461, 462.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Three of the Act's sub-headings. ss 421 to 424 are the fraudulent dispositions,
-- which turn on defeating creditors or concealing property rather than on taking
-- anything. s 425 defines mischief and ss 427 to 440 aggravate it. s 441 defines
-- criminal trespass, s 442 makes house-breaking a species of it, and ss 449 to 462
-- aggravate that.
--
-- This module closes the dependency recorded as T2 in
-- `registers/verification-register-pass-4.md`: s 104(5) of Chapter 4A continues the
-- right of private defence of property against house-breaking, and until now
-- house-breaking was defined nowhere in this encoding. It is s 442, and it is here.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. ss 426, 447, 448 and 458A are punishment sections and
-- are not encoded. ss 438, 439 and 462 are encoded despite being framed as
-- punishment provisions, because each states a distinct combination of facts.

§§ `Sections 421 to 424 -- Fraudulent deeds and dispositions of property`

-- s 421: dishonestly or fraudulently removing, concealing, delivering or
-- transferring property without adequate consideration, intending or knowing it
-- likely that this will prevent its distribution among creditors.
-- s 422: dishonestly or fraudulently preventing a debt due to oneself or another
-- from being made available for payment of debts.
-- s 423: dishonestly or fraudulently signing or executing a deed of transfer or
-- charge containing a false statement as to the consideration, or as to the person
-- for whose benefit it is really intended to operate.
-- s 424: dishonestly or fraudulently concealing or removing property, or assisting
-- in that, or dishonestly releasing a demand or claim to which one is entitled.
--
-- Each of the four is complete in itself; none builds on another.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 421"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulent removal of property to prevent distribution among creditors under Penal Code 1871 section 421
GIVEN d IS A `Fraudulent Deed` @desc Dishonest or fraudulent removal, concealment, delivery or transfer of property without adequate consideration, intending or knowing it likely to prevent distribution among creditors.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulent removal to defeat creditors` IF
        d's `dishonestly or fraudulently removes conceals or delivers to any person or transfers or causes to be transferred to any person without adequate consideration any property`
    AND d's `intending thereby to prevent or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 422"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulently preventing a debt from being available to creditors under Penal Code 1871 section 422
GIVEN d IS A `Fraudulent Deed` @desc Dishonestly or fraudulently preventing a debt or demand due to oneself or another from being made available for payment of debts.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulently preventing a debt being available` IF
    d's `dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of that other person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 423"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulent execution of a deed containing a false statement of consideration under Penal Code 1871 section 423
GIVEN d IS A `Fraudulent Deed` @desc Dishonestly or fraudulently signing, executing or becoming a party to a deed of transfer or charge containing a false statement as to consideration or as to the person really benefited.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulent execution of a deed` IF
        d's `dishonestly or fraudulently signs executes or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property or any interest in it`
    AND d's `the deed or instrument contains a false statement relating to the consideration for the transfer or charge or relating to the person for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 424"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulent concealment of property or release of a claim under Penal Code 1871 section 424
GIVEN d IS A `Fraudulent Deed` @desc Dishonest or fraudulent concealment or removal of property, assisting in it, or dishonestly releasing a demand or claim to which one is entitled.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulent concealment or release of a claim` IF
        d's `dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person or assists in the concealment or removal of it`
    OR  d's `dishonestly releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled`

§§ `Section 425 -- Mischief`

-- Whoever, with intent to cause or knowing that he is likely to cause wrongful loss
-- or damage to the public or any person, causes the destruction of any property, or
-- such change in it or in its situation as destroys or diminishes its value or
-- utility or affects it injuriously.
--
-- Explanation 1 provides that it is not essential that the offender intend loss to
-- the OWNER of the property -- wrongful loss to any person by injuring any property
-- is enough, whether it belongs to that person or not. Explanation 2 extends the
-- section to property belonging to the offender, or to him and others jointly. Both
-- widen what may be asserted and neither adds a limb; the facts as worded already
-- carry them.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 425"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief under Penal Code 1871 section 425
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Intent or knowledge of causing wrongful loss or damage, together with destruction of property or a change in it that destroys or diminishes its value or utility or affects it injuriously.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief` IF
        m's `with intent to cause or knowing that he is likely to cause wrongful loss or damage to the public or any person`
    AND m's `causes the destruction of any property or such change in any property or in the situation of it as destroys or diminishes its value or utility or affects it injuriously`

§§ `Sections 427 to 440 -- Aggravated mischief`

-- s 427: mischief causing, or likely to cause, a disruption to a key service or to
-- the Government's or a public agency's duties, functions or powers. s 427(2)
-- defines "key service" and "public agency" by a list; both are carried inside the
-- disruption facts rather than enumerated.
-- s 428: mischief by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal.
-- s 435: mischief by fire or explosive, intending or knowing it likely to cause
-- damage to property.
-- s 436: the same, intending or knowing it likely to cause the destruction of a
-- building of one of the listed kinds.
-- s 437: mischief to a decked vessel or one of 20 tons or upwards, intending or
-- knowing it likely to destroy or render it unsafe.
-- s 438: the s 437 mischief committed, OR ATTEMPTED, by fire or explosive. The
-- attempt is expressly within the section, so no separate s 511 analysis is needed.
-- s 439: intentionally running a vessel aground or ashore, intending theft or
-- misappropriation of property in it. Note this section does not require mischief at
-- all -- it stands on its own conduct and intent.
-- s 440: mischief committed after preparation for causing death, hurt or wrongful
-- restraint, or fear of them.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 427"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief causing disruption to a key service under Penal Code 1871 section 427
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief by an act causing, or known to be likely to cause, disruption to a key service or to the Government's or a public agency's functions.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief disrupting a key service` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND (   m's `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the provision of any key service`
         OR m's `the act causes or the accused knows it is likely to cause a disruption to the performance of any duty or function of or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 428"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief by killing or maiming an animal under Penal Code 1871 section 428
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief committed by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief to an animal` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND m's `commits the mischief by killing poisoning maiming or rendering useless any animal`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 435"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief by fire or explosive with intent to cause damage under Penal Code 1871 section 435
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief by fire or explosive substance, intending or knowing it likely to cause damage to property.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief by fire to cause damage` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND m's `commits the mischief by fire or any explosive substance`
    AND m's `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause damage to any property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 436"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief by fire or explosive with intent to destroy a house under Penal Code 1871 section 436
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief by fire or explosive substance, intending or knowing it likely to destroy a building of one of the kinds listed in s 436.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief by fire to destroy a building` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND m's `commits the mischief by fire or any explosive substance`
    AND m's `intending to cause or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause the destruction of a building ordinarily used as a place of worship for the administration of justice for the transaction of public affairs for education or art for public use or ornament as a human dwelling or as a place for the custody of property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 437"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief to a decked vessel under Penal Code 1871 section 437
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief to a decked vessel or one of 20 tons or upwards, intending or knowing it likely to destroy or render it unsafe.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief to a vessel` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND m's `commits the mischief to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards intending to destroy or render unsafe or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe that vessel`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 438"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief to a vessel by fire or explosive under Penal Code 1871 section 438
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc The s 437 mischief, committed or attempted by fire or explosive substance. The attempt is within the section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief to a vessel by fire` IF
        m's `commits or attempts to commit that mischief to the vessel by fire or any explosive substance`
    AND m's `commits the mischief to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards intending to destroy or render unsafe or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe that vessel`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 439"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes running a vessel aground with intent to commit theft under Penal Code 1871 section 439
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Intentionally running a vessel aground or ashore, intending theft or misappropriation of property in it. This section does not require mischief.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes running a vessel aground to commit theft` IF
    m's `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore intending to commit theft of property contained in it or dishonestly to misappropriate any such property or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 440"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes mischief committed after preparation for causing death or hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 440
GIVEN m IS A Mischief @desc Mischief committed after preparation for causing death, hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of them.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes mischief after preparation for causing hurt` IF
        `constitutes mischief` m
    AND m's `having made preparation for causing to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of death hurt or wrongful restraint`

§§ `Sections 441 and 442 -- Criminal trespass and house-breaking`

-- s 441: entering into or upon property in the possession of another with intent to
-- commit an offence or to intimidate, insult or annoy the person in possession; OR
-- having lawfully entered, unlawfully remaining there with either of those intents.
-- The two conduct limbs are alternatives and the two intents are alternatives, so
-- the rule is a conjunction of two disjunctions.
--
-- s 442: criminal trespass by entering into, or remaining in, a building, tent,
-- container or vessel used as a human dwelling, or a building used as a place for
-- worship or for the custody of property. Its Explanation makes the introduction of
-- any part of the body sufficient entry, which widens the conduct fact and adds no
-- limb.
--
-- s 442 is what s 104(5) of Chapter 4A needed. `NOTES.md` §3 records that
-- house-breaking is an aggravated criminal trespass and so falls within the s 104(1)
-- list; with this section encoded, that containment can now be seen rather than
-- merely stated.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 441"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes criminal trespass under Penal Code 1871 section 441
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc Entering, or unlawfully remaining after a lawful entry, on property in another's possession, with intent to commit an offence or to intimidate, insult or annoy the possessor.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes criminal trespass` IF
        (   tp's `enters into or upon property in the possession of another`
         OR tp's `having lawfully entered into or upon such property unlawfully remains there`)
    AND (   tp's `with intent to commit an offence`
         OR tp's `with intent to intimidate insult or annoy any person in possession of the property`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 442"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking under Penal Code 1871 section 442
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc Criminal trespass by entering or remaining in a dwelling, place of worship or place for the custody of property. Any part of the body entering is sufficient.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking` IF
        `constitutes criminal trespass` tp
    AND tp's `the property entered or remained in is a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or a building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property`

§§ `Sections 449 to 453 -- House-breaking for a purpose, and going equipped`

-- ss 449, 450 and 451 are house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable
-- with death, with imprisonment for life, and with imprisonment respectively. The
-- three are a graded series on the seriousness of the intended offence.
-- s 452 is house-breaking after preparation for causing hurt, assault or wrongful
-- restraint, or fear of them.
-- s 453 is different in kind: it punishes being found armed, disguised or equipped,
-- and requires no trespass at all. s 453(2) shifts the burden to the accused to show
-- lawful authority or purpose on the first limb -- a rule about proof, and the
-- "without lawful authority or a lawful purpose" wording is already inside the fact.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 449"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking to commit an offence punishable with death under Penal Code 1871 section 449
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking committed in order to commit an offence punishable with death.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking to commit a capital offence` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 450"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life under Penal Code 1871 section 450
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking committed in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking to commit a life-imprisonment offence` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 451"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment under Penal Code 1871 section 451
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking committed in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking to commit an imprisonable offence` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `commits the house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 452"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking after preparation for causing hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 452
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking after preparation for causing hurt, assaulting, wrongfully restraining, or putting a person in fear of those.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking after preparation for hurt` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person for assaulting any person for wrongfully restraining any person or for putting any person in fear of hurt assault or wrongful restraint`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 453"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession of house-breaking implements or offensive weapons under Penal Code 1871 section 453
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc Being found armed without lawful authority or purpose, disguised with intent to commit an offence, or equipped for house-breaking. No trespass is required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes going equipped for house-breaking` IF
        tp's `is found armed with any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting or any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death without lawful authority or a lawful purpose`
    OR  tp's `is found having his face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit any offence`
    OR  tp's `is found equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking`

§§ `Sections 459 to 462 -- Hurt in house-breaking, and closed receptacles`

-- s 459: grievous hurt caused, or death or grievous hurt attempted, while committing
-- house-breaking.
-- s 460: the same harm caused by any person guilty of the house-breaking, fixing
-- EVERY person jointly concerned in it -- so joint concern is an alternative route
-- into the section and not a further requirement.
-- s 461: dishonestly, or with intent to commit mischief, breaking open or unfastening
-- a closed receptacle containing or believed to contain property.
-- s 462: the same act by a person entrusted with the receptacle and without authority
-- to open it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 459"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing grievous hurt while committing house-breaking under Penal Code 1871 section 459
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking in the course of which grievous hurt is caused, or death or grievous hurt attempted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes grievous hurt in house-breaking` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `while committing the house-breaking causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 460"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes house-breaking where death or grievous hurt is caused under Penal Code 1871 section 460
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc House-breaking where a person guilty of it causes or attempts death or grievous hurt. Every person jointly concerned is within the section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes house-breaking with death or grievous hurt` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` tp
    AND tp's `at the time of the house-breaking a person guilty of it voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 461"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes dishonestly breaking open a closed receptacle under Penal Code 1871 section 461
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc Dishonestly, or with intent to commit mischief, breaking open or unfastening a closed receptacle containing or believed to contain property.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes breaking open a closed receptacle` IF
    tp's `dishonestly or with intent to commit mischief breaks open or unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 462"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes breaking open a closed receptacle by a person entrusted with it under Penal Code 1871 section 462
GIVEN tp IS A Trespass @desc The s 461 act, by a person entrusted with the receptacle and having no authority to open it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes breaking open a receptacle entrusted to the accused` IF
        `constitutes breaking open a closed receptacle` tp
    AND tp's `is entrusted with that closed receptacle without having authority to open it`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a fraudulent disposition` IF
        (   `constitutes fraudulent removal to defeat creditors` (a's `fraudulent deed`)
         OR `constitutes fraudulently preventing a debt being available` (a's `fraudulent deed`)
         OR `constitutes fraudulent execution of a deed` (a's `fraudulent deed`)
         OR `constitutes fraudulent concealment or release of a claim` (a's `fraudulent deed`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes mischief` IF
        (   `constitutes mischief` (a's `mischief`)
         OR `constitutes running a vessel aground to commit theft` (a's `mischief`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes criminal trespass` IF
        `constitutes criminal trespass` (a's `trespass`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes house-breaking` IF
        `constitutes house-breaking` (a's `trespass`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes going equipped for house-breaking` IF
        `constitutes going equipped for house-breaking` (a's `trespass`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
